commit ae5edb643b33fe7d759bb71d148473dffb12e6b6
Author: Tyler Gannon <tyler@pagerguild.com>
Date:   Wed Aug 19 14:03:45 2026 -0600

    Recover agy branches from artifact-path declaration failures

    The agy CLI's native write_to_file tool writes workspace files
    successfully but its end-of-turn permission declaration rejects any
    path outside ~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/<uuid>/, failing the whole
    turn and taking down parallel runs whose other branches had already
    completed. Detect that error signature in RunTurn and spend one bounded
    repair turn — resuming the same conversation — instructing the model to
    redo its file writes via shell only. A second failure still propagates.

    Regression tests pin the detector against the recorded error text and
    prove the repair is attempted exactly once. Run evidence, summary, and
    independent validation records under ephemeral/.

